Subject: Tweak: no HUD
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84

For clean recordings and screenshots (issue #58), "No HUD" starts matches
without their overlays; the host's H key shows or hides them during a match
(mscharged_tweak_hud_frame takes its presses once a frame). Hidden are the
scoreboard (hud_2.fen: team icons, clock, items, captain ability meter) with
its score numbers (NumberDisplay, also a Mega Strike's goal count), the player
number badges, ball-carrier arrows and screen-edge markers (Indicators), the
REPLAY caption (ingame_text.fen), the goal's lower third (goal_overlay.fen)
and the captain's super ability card.

Only their drawing is skipped: FERender::RenderScene leaves out those scenes,
NumberDisplay::Render and DrawIndicator return before they attach anything.
The overlays, numbers and markers still update as in the original, so the
game, replays and online matches are unchanged. The Mega Strike meter and the
goalie's Mega Strike defence targets and countdown stay, as players need them
to play; so do the pause menu, the screens after a match and the lessons'
ticker. The guarded hooks exist only in the opt-in native game module.

